// The SIGNATURE half: a declaration that NAMES a raw pointer must carry the marker, so a reader greps the
// declaration instead of opening the body. A `contract` member is exempt — it is bodiless, and both its
// implementer and its caller are forced by their own types.
fn int32 peek(UnsafePtr<int32> p) { return 0; }

fn int32 main() { return 0; }
